      "fund": "Substack / Rebound Capital",
      "date": "June 09, 2026",
      "summary": "Rebound Capital evaluates Lululemon following an ~80% drawdown from its 2024 peak, analyzing flat-to-declining Americas same-store sales (-5% comps in Q1 FY26) alongside executive turnover and founder proxy battles . They detail Lululemon's direct-to-consumer high-margin model (54-56% gross margins) and zero-debt balance sheet ($1.5B cash), emphasizing that aggressive stock buybacks and rapid international expansion\u2014particularly 20%+ China growth\u2014provide asymmetric upside as North American inventory and product lines refresh.",
      "url": "https://reboundcapital.substack.com/p/deep-dive-lululemon-lulu"
    },
