      "title": "Lululemon Stock Analysis: Revenues Have tripled, but the Market Cap is Stuck in... 2019",
      "fund": "Substack / Quality Stocks",
      "date": "March 15, 2026",
      "summary": "Quality Stocks applies its GARP framework to Lululemon, examining how valuation compressed to a ~15x P/E reset to 2019 levels despite revenue tripling over the same period. The analysis details unit economics driven by the low-cost 'Community Ambassador Program' rather than traditional celebrity ad spend, resulting in returns on capital near ~38%. Catalysts focus on executing the 'Power of Three x2' plan to double international revenue led by Greater China and stabilizing North American market share under incoming leadership.",
      "url": "https://qualitystocks.substack.com/p/lululemon-stock-analysis"
    },
    {
      "title": "Lululemon \u2013 Cheap for a Reason",
      "fund": "Substack / Rijnberk InvestInsights",
      "date": "December 27, 2025",
      "summary": "Daan of Rijnberk InvestInsights presents a critical value perspective, arguing that Lululemon's core US market is experiencing structural brand fatigue, stale product assortments, and margin compression. The memo notes minimal switching costs in activewear and aggressive competition from Vuori and Alo, but highlights a major governance catalyst in Elliott Investment Management taking a $1B+ activist stake to demand board restructuring, operational discipline, and CEO succession.",
      "url": "https://rijnberkinvestinsights.substack.com/p/lululemon-cheap-for-a-reason"
    },
