      "fund": "r/ValueInvesting",
      "date": "September 11, 2025",
      "summary": "A detailed value-oriented post on r/ValueInvesting framing Lululemon as a high-moat compounder trading at 11.4x trailing earnings ($167/share) due to fixable North American execution issues. The author highlights elite unit economics including 42% ROE, 38% ROIC, 58%+ gross margins, and zero long-term debt. Key operational catalysts required to hit the $300 fair value estimate include Americas comp store sales returning to positive territory, gross margin stabilization above 58%, and China revenue growth exceeding 15% annually.",
